{#
  « Vérification des capacités », moved as it was from the single page this
  module used to have onto the dashboard (issue #843, IT-01): same data
  (Service\SlotService::capacityBreakdownForYear()), same rendering.
  Requires `selected_year`, `is_past_year`, `waitlist_enabled` and
  `capacity_breakdown` in scope.
#}
<div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h5 mb-3">Vérification des capacités — année {{ selected_year.label }}</h2>
        {# The projected headcount (and therefore the remaining places and
           the public level derived from it) is computed on TODAY's
           members: those three columns only mean something for a year to
           come. On a past year they would show today's projection
           presented as a figure of that time. #}
        {% if is_past_year %}
            <p class="small text-body-secondary">
                Année passée (consultation) : l'effectif projeté, le restant et le niveau public ne sont pas
                affichés — ce sont des projections, elles n'ont de sens que pour une année à venir. La capacité
                et les demandes acceptées, elles, sont bien historiques.
            </p>
        {% endif %}
        {# « Restant » and « Niveau public » describe the availability the
           public is told about: without waitlist management there is
           nothing to tell, so both columns are absent rather than filled
           with figures nobody uses. The stored values do not move:
           switching the waitlist back on brings them back unchanged. #}
        {% set show_waitlist_columns = not is_past_year and waitlist_enabled %}
        {% if not waitlist_enabled %}
            <p class="small text-body-secondary">
                La gestion des listes d'attente est désactivée : le restant et le niveau vu par le public
                ne sont pas calculés. Vous pouvez la réactiver dans Réglages, encart « Capacités par branche ».
            </p>
        {% endif %}
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm align-middle">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Branche</th>
                        <th>Année</th>
                        <th>Capacité</th>
                        {% if not is_past_year %}<th>Effectif projeté</th>{% endif %}
                        <th>Demandes acceptées</th>
                        {% if show_waitlist_columns %}
                            <th>Restant</th>
                            <th>Niveau public</th>
                        {% endif %}
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    {% for row in capacity_breakdown %}
                        <tr>
                            <td>{{ row.branch_label }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.year_in_branch }}<sup>e</sup></td>
                            {# A null capacity is "no limit", never "0": printing the raw
                               number would make an unconfigured branch read as a closed
                               one, exactly the mistake the nullable column exists to
                               prevent. A 0 itself does print as 0. #}
                            <td>{% if row.capacity is null %}<span class="text-body-secondary">Sans limite</span>{% else %}{{ row.capacity }}{% endif %}</td>
                            {% if not is_past_year %}<td>{{ row.projected }}</td>{% endif %}
                            <td>{{ row.accepted }}</td>
                            {% if show_waitlist_columns %}
                                <td>{% if row.remaining is null %}<span class="text-body-secondary">—</span>{% else %}{{ row.remaining }}{% endif %}</td>
                                <td>
                                    {% if row.tier is null %}
                                        <span class="badge text-bg-secondary">Sans limite</span>
                                    {% elseif row.tier == 'available' %}
                                        <span class="badge text-bg-success">Disponible</span>
                                    {% elseif row.tier == 'limited' %}
                                        <span class="badge text-bg-warning">Attente limitée</span>
                                    {% else %}
                                        <span class="badge text-bg-danger">Attente importante</span>
                                    {% endif %}
                                </td>
                            {% endif %}
                        </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
